[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds every report about a wrong date and calls them one issue with
one fix queued. The reports describe two problems, and one fix covers only the first. Each
problem now has its own ticket:

- `parser`: [#1](https://github.com/dandezmirean/support-kb/issues/1)
- `hint`: [#2](https://github.com/dandezmirean/support-kb/issues/2)

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## parser

The shared parser reads every date month first. All our tenants write the day first, so a
booking for 2 March comes out as 3 February. This covers app and email reports from every
tenant, and form reports from tenants on booking-v2. Ticket
[#1](https://github.com/dandezmirean/support-kb/issues/1) covers this whole row, including the
reports in the note under the table.

The reports in the note under the table have no day and month swapped. The booking lands one
day early, or on a different day depending on where the reader is: "Client in Lisbon got
Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." That may be a time zone bug. The desk files them under
`parser` by tenant and counts them there, so [#1](https://github.com/dandezmirean/support-kb/issues/1)
covers them until someone shows they need a fix of their own.

## hint

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type the month first, as
the hint tells them, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. A parser fix
leaves these broken. The hint has to change. Only tenants on booking-v3 who book through the
form hit it. The table above still marks this row as having no ticket of its own. It has one
now: [#2](https://github.com/dandezmirean/support-kb/issues/2).

The tenant and the channel decide a report's cause (`causes.ts`). Intake's tag guesses from the
reporter's browser and disagrees with the cause often, so this page does not use it.

